{"type":"text","timestamp":1794342417638,"sessionID":"ses_e38e260b1ffeHzblIyyPT60RUy","part":{"id":"prt_1c72474d00010C6P6UC1Rs3VeL","messageID":"msg_1c7245a1b001GhMm2iI1FxzUM2","sessionID":"ses_e38e260b1ffeHzblIyyPT60RUy","type":"text","text":"Done. The image gallery is complete and verified end-to-end.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): Flask app with SQLite under `./data`, bearer-token auth (register/login/`sessions` table), content-sniffed PNG/JPEG detection, per-uploader file storage, and paged listing — all API contract points confirmed working (201/200/401/403/404/409/204 status codes, unchanged bytes with correct content type).\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`): React + TypeScript with Tailwind v4 (via `@tailwindcss/vite`, no hand-written CSS except the entry `index.css`). Sign-in/register, signed-in username + sign-out, responsive thumbnail grid with paging + empty state, full-size viewer with filename/title/size, upload form with PNG/JPEG preview + API error surface, and confirmed delete on own images.\n\n**Verification**: all 20+ API scenarios passed via Flask test client, frontend `npm run build` succeeds, and static/SPA serving works. Added a `.gitignore` (node_modules, dist, `__pycache__`, `.venv`, `data/`) and moved `tailwindcss`/`@tailwindcss/vite` to devDependencies.\n\nNote: I couldn't run the full Docker build (no Docker in the sandbox), but the `Dockerfile`'s `npm ci` + `pip install` + `gunicorn` flow is unchanged and matches the existing lockfiles.","time":{"start":1794342417616,"end":1794342417619}}}
